246
00:15:09.868 --> 00:15:12.079
I-I spoke to Nat on the phone.

247
00:15:12.829 --> 00:15:14.998
She and Zack are. uh. at home.

248
00:15:16.708 --> 00:15:17.709
Both are okay.

249
00:15:18.252 --> 00:15:19.253
[chuckles]

250
00:15:19.336 --> 00:15:20.546
How are you? How's your hand?

251
00:15:21.296 --> 00:15:22.297
I'll heal.

252
00:15:23.131 --> 00:15:24.550
Or I'll get a hook.

253
00:15:24.633 --> 00:15:26.176
[both chuckle]

254
00:15:29.221 --> 00:15:30.347
I'm so sorry.

255
00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:34.268
[sighs]

256
00:15:36.436 --> 00:15:37.437
I saw the video.

257
00:15:39.314 --> 00:15:40.482
It was really brave.

258
00:15:41.733 --> 00:15:42.734
We got him.

259
00:15:44.611 --> 00:15:45.612
Yeah.

260
00:15:50.951 --> 00:15:52.411
So what do we do now?

261
00:15:54.705 --> 00:15:55.706
[Tom sighs]

262
00:16:00.085 --> 00:16:01.503
Well. let's just get you home.

263
00:16:02.171 --> 00:16:03.172
And then?

264
00:16:13.765 --> 00:16:16.685
- I know I fucked up. Tom. I...
- [Tom] No. [stammers]

265
00:16:17.436 --> 00:16:20.606
I'm not putting this all on you.

266
00:16:22.983 --> 00:16:24.067
I. uh...

267
00:16:26.904 --> 00:16:29.406
[Anna] I'm glad that you know the truth.

268
00:16:35.996 --> 00:16:36.997
I love you.

269
00:16:49.885 --> 00:16:50.969
[speaker beeps]

270
00:16:51.053 --> 00:16:52.471
[announcer] <i>Due to Hurricane Wesley.</i>

271
00:16:52.554 --> 00:16:55.182
<i>Savannah is now under
immediate evacuation order.</i>

272
00:16:55.265 --> 00:16:57.351
<i>Those who can leave should.</i>

273
00:16:57.434 --> 00:16:58.602
Oh. Lord.

274
00:16:58.685 --> 00:17:01.021
Yeah. let's just
get me out of here. right?

275
00:17:06.944 --> 00:17:09.195
[thunder rumbling]

276
00:17:17.371 --> 00:17:19.414
[radio chatter]

277
00:17:20.123 --> 00:17:22.125
[officer] Every jail in the county
just went into lockdown.

278
00:17:22.209 --> 00:17:23.669
so settle in. We got a long ride.

279
00:17:23.752 --> 00:17:26.128
Sir. Officer. please.

280
00:17:26.213 --> 00:17:27.214
[officer] What's the problem?

281
00:17:27.297 --> 00:17:30.425
I-I get seizures and I-I need my medicine.

282
00:17:30.509 --> 00:17:33.554
It's in my pocket right here. please. sir.
Please. I can't take it out.

283
00:17:33.637 --> 00:17:35.639
- [car door opens]
- Thank you. sir.

284
00:17:37.808 --> 00:17:38.809
[car door closes]

285
00:17:57.828 --> 00:17:58.829
[Anna] Natalie.

286
00:17:59.413 --> 00:18:00.789
Zack.

287
00:18:00.873 --> 00:18:02.124
- [Natalie breathing shakily]
- Hi. Mom.

288
00:18:02.207 --> 00:18:03.709
- [Natalie] Hey.
- Hi.

289
00:18:05.502 --> 00:18:08.213
[Anna] You're home. You're safe.
[breathes shakily]

290
00:18:09.923 --> 00:18:11.425
Mom. what happened to your hand?

291
00:18:12.217 --> 00:18:13.218
Hey.

292
00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:17.931
I was lucky that I didn't lose a finger.
honey. [chuckles]

293
00:18:19.683 --> 00:18:21.185
Why did you run away. huh?

294
00:18:22.102 --> 00:18:24.229
- I wanted to come home.
- [sniffles]

295
00:18:24.313 --> 00:18:25.731
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

296
00:18:28.108 --> 00:18:29.860
- I'm okay. I...
- Okay.

297
00:18:29.943 --> 00:18:31.528
[Zack] Sorry. just give me a moment.

298
00:18:33.697 --> 00:18:35.782
- [Natalie breathes shakily]
- [Anna sighs]

299
00:18:37.284 --> 00:18:38.285
[sighs]

300
00:18:43.749 --> 00:18:45.626
[thunder rumbling]

301
00:18:50.631 --> 00:18:52.841
Hey. mind if I...

302
00:19:02.184 --> 00:19:05.687
Zack. when I was locked up
and had no idea where you were

303
00:19:05.771 --> 00:19:06.897
or what happened to you...

304
00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.025
It is Zack. right?

305
00:19:12.319 --> 00:19:13.320
Yeah.

306
00:19:14.571 --> 00:19:15.572
It's me.

307
00:19:17.115 --> 00:19:21.119
You don't need to be scared. Or anything...

308
00:19:22.955 --> 00:19:24.039
[Tom sighs]

309
00:19:25.082 --> 00:19:29.503
You know. um.
when my brother was struggling...

310
00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.215
he buried it all

311
00:19:34.883 --> 00:19:36.885
and none of us knew how bad it was.

312
00:19:44.685 --> 00:19:47.437
He didn't die in an accident.

313
00:19:49.857 --> 00:19:52.109
It was just something
my parents told people.

314
00:19:54.111 --> 00:19:56.697
And I was 14. so I copied 'em. right?

315
00:19:58.115 --> 00:19:59.867
Why are you telling me now?

316
00:20:01.326 --> 00:20:03.287
[Tom] Well. I guess for a long time.

317
00:20:04.538 --> 00:20:09.418
I didn't wanna see
how bad things were with you.

318
00:20:12.045 --> 00:20:17.885
It was easier for me
to just tell myself you'd get better.

319
00:20:19.011 --> 00:20:20.012
[Tom sighs]

320
00:20:22.556 --> 00:20:25.225
But sometimes things just

321
00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:27.895
suck.

322
00:20:27.978 --> 00:20:31.982
And we can't pretend otherwise.

323
00:20:32.065 --> 00:20:35.319
We'll just get through it together.

324
00:20:39.448 --> 00:20:41.283
I don't know what you want me to say.

325
00:20:46.997 --> 00:20:48.749
[knocks on door]

326
00:20:52.377 --> 00:20:53.462
Who did I kill this time?

327
00:20:54.046 --> 00:20:56.423
Yeah. about that whole thing.

328
00:20:56.507 --> 00:20:57.966
Where's Max?

329
00:20:58.050 --> 00:20:59.259
[Grayson] Can we come in?

330
00:21:00.761 --> 00:21:01.803
Yeah.

331
00:21:07.309 --> 00:21:08.393
Max assaulted a cop.

332
00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:12.439
Escaped from custody
a couple of hours ago.

333
00:21:12.523 --> 00:21:14.691
[Grayson] I don't guess he'd be
dumb enough to come right back.

334
00:21:14.775 --> 00:21:16.443
but given the issues between y'all

335
00:21:16.527 --> 00:21:19.780
and the injuries
that he inflicted on our fellow officer.

336
00:21:20.572 --> 00:21:21.740
better safe than sorry.

337
00:21:21.823 --> 00:21:23.075
How long have y'all been home?

338
00:21:23.742 --> 00:21:25.911
Uh. not long.

339
00:21:25.994 --> 00:21:27.037
[electricity crackles]

340
00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:28.705
[Grayson]
Hurricane Wes ain't fucking around.

341
00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:33.502
You mind if we make sure
nobody's playing hide-and-seek?

342
00:21:34.628 --> 00:21:36.797
- [Tom] No.
- [detective] Here.

343
00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:38.382
You. upstairs. You. that way.

344
00:21:40.551 --> 00:21:43.887
Listen. um.
I don't know if Cady killed his wife.

345
00:21:43.971 --> 00:21:47.975
but I guess it's pretty clear
he set out to make y'all's life hell.

346
00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:51.270
So. sorry we fucked up.

347
00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:56.441
Let's make sure y'all are safe
and get the heck out of here.

348
00:21:59.069 --> 00:22:02.072
[Anna] Nat. Zack. pack a bag.
We're getting out of here.

349
00:22:03.866 --> 00:22:05.117
[thunder rumbles]

350
00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:07.202
[tense music playing]

351
00:22:21.884 --> 00:22:22.885
[phone chimes]

352
00:22:41.737 --> 00:22:43.739
Hey. can I talk to you upstairs
for a second?

353
00:22:46.241 --> 00:22:48.243
[police radio chatter]

354
00:22:54.499 --> 00:22:56.960
Just game this out with me.

355
00:22:57.044 --> 00:22:59.755
We move to a different state.
change our names.

356
00:22:59.838 --> 00:23:02.090
- just wait for him to find us.
- [keypad beeping]

357
00:23:02.174 --> 00:23:03.592
[Anna] What are you saying?

358
00:23:07.137 --> 00:23:09.139
[Tom] You take the kids out of town.
I'll wait for him.

359
00:23:11.517 --> 00:23:12.851
You're just going to kill him?

360
00:23:13.393 --> 00:23:16.021
Eliminate the threat. For good.

361
00:23:17.189 --> 00:23:18.565
- [door shuts]
- [keypad beeps]

362
00:23:18.649 --> 00:23:19.650
What if he kills you?

363
00:23:19.733 --> 00:23:22.402
- Have you considered that possibility?
- He is already killing us.

364
00:23:23.111 --> 00:23:24.321
Death by a thousand cuts.

365
00:23:24.404 --> 00:23:27.824
No. we have real evidence now.
Max Cady's going to prison.

366
00:23:27.908 --> 00:23:29.201
[Tom] When?

367
00:23:29.284 --> 00:23:30.285
He won't stop.

368
00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:36.792
This fear that we're living with.
this will be our life and our kids' lives.

369
00:23:38.752 --> 00:23:39.753
[Grayson] Y'all in here?

370
00:23:41.088 --> 00:23:44.883
[sighs] Oh. you got your shotgun.
Can't say I blame you.

371
00:23:45.926 --> 00:23:48.178
Well. you have a very angry possum
living under your porch.

372
00:23:48.262 --> 00:23:50.264
but no Max Cady.

373
00:24:05.153 --> 00:24:06.905
[wind whistling]

374
00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:19.126
Listen. keep your alarm on
and leave town as soon as you can.

375
00:24:19.710 --> 00:24:20.919
The storm's only getting worse.

376
00:24:21.003 --> 00:24:24.131
We're just gonna throw some stuff
in a bag and be gone in 15 minutes.

377
00:24:24.214 --> 00:24:25.215
All right. good.

378
00:24:40.606 --> 00:24:43.442
[menacing music playing]

379
00:24:48.280 --> 00:24:50.657
[thunderclap]

380
00:24:56.163 --> 00:24:58.373
[wind howling outside]

381
00:25:03.962 --> 00:25:04.963
[thuds]

382
00:25:09.218 --> 00:25:11.011
[footsteps]

383
00:25:14.264 --> 00:25:16.141
[footsteps continue]

384
00:25:39.456 --> 00:25:40.582
[thudding]

385
00:25:41.542 --> 00:25:43.293
[wind whistling]

386
00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:58.976
[wind roaring]

387
00:26:11.905 --> 00:26:13.156
Guys?

388
00:26:15.200 --> 00:26:16.368
You all packed?

389
00:26:22.499 --> 00:26:23.500
Nat?

390
00:26:25.127 --> 00:26:26.336
- [wind whistling]
- [rain falling]

391
00:26:26.420 --> 00:26:27.421
Nat?

392
00:26:30.883 --> 00:26:33.218
- Tom!
- [laughs]

393
00:26:33.302 --> 00:26:34.595
- Tom!
- [Tom grunts]

394
00:26:34.678 --> 00:26:37.556
[grunts] Let him go! Let go of him!

395
00:26:37.639 --> 00:26:39.057
- [Max] Gun down.
- [Tom] Let go!

396
00:26:39.141 --> 00:26:40.267
Gun down!

397
00:26:40.934 --> 00:26:42.811
If you hurt him. he will shoot.

398
00:26:42.895 --> 00:26:45.230
- [screaming]
- Go on. Do it.

399
00:26:45.856 --> 00:26:47.900
Hey. hey. hey. hey. hey. hey!
Okay. okay. okay!

400
00:26:47.983 --> 00:26:49.443
Gun down!

401
00:26:50.068 --> 00:26:51.069
Now!

402
00:26:53.447 --> 00:26:54.948
Back. Back!

403
00:27:03.248 --> 00:27:04.541
[exclaims]

404
00:27:04.625 --> 00:27:06.668
- Hey. hey. hey. hey! Come on! Stop!
- [whimpers]

405
00:27:06.752 --> 00:27:08.045
- [Max] All right.
- [Tom] Okay...

406
00:27:08.128 --> 00:27:10.964
- [Anna exclaims]
- [Max] Oh. okay.

407
00:27:12.049 --> 00:27:15.636
On the count of four. let's proceed.

408
00:27:19.515 --> 00:27:21.391
- Over there. Over there.
- Okay.

409
00:27:21.475 --> 00:27:25.938
All right.
Ms. Deveraux and Mr. Prosecutor.

410
00:27:26.021 --> 00:27:27.606
please be seated.

411
00:27:27.689 --> 00:27:29.149
Sit the fuck down. There.

412
00:27:29.233 --> 00:27:30.234
Those two.

413
00:27:31.026 --> 00:27:32.069
Right.

414
00:27:32.152 --> 00:27:36.156
Now. here. Their wrists to the chair.

415
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:38.742
- Boy. stay there.
- It's okay.

416
00:27:38.825 --> 00:27:40.285
[Max] Nice and tight.

417
00:27:40.994 --> 00:27:42.538
Come on. Come on.

418
00:27:42.621 --> 00:27:44.831
To the chairs. Come on.

419
00:27:44.915 --> 00:27:46.875
All right. stand up. Stand up.

420
00:27:46.959 --> 00:27:49.378
Now. you. her wrists.

421
00:27:52.005 --> 00:27:53.423
Please don't do this. Dad.

422
00:27:53.507 --> 00:27:56.844
Dad? You said "Dad"?
Okay. say. "<i>Papá. Papá.</i>"

423
00:27:57.970 --> 00:28:00.722
Just take me with you.
I-I'll go anywhere you want.

424
00:28:01.515 --> 00:28:03.350
- You said you wanted to help me. right?
- Natalie.

425
00:28:03.433 --> 00:28:06.144
Yeah. I said something like that. yeah.
but then you shot me.

426
00:28:06.228 --> 00:28:09.147
Okay. turn the fuck around now.
You're gonna sit here.

427
00:28:10.274 --> 00:28:11.567
All right.

428
00:28:11.650 --> 00:28:12.651
Now.

429
00:28:13.819 --> 00:28:17.197
we better make sure
he's not a danger to himself.

430
00:28:17.281 --> 00:28:18.448
- No.
- No.

431
00:28:18.532 --> 00:28:19.533
No. no. no. no. Max.

432
00:28:19.616 --> 00:28:21.785
- You don't have to do that. No!
- [Anna] No. No. Zack!

433
00:28:21.869 --> 00:28:24.037
- [Max] All right. Come here.
- [Anna] Zack. I'm right here.

434
00:28:24.121 --> 00:28:25.163
- [Max] There.
- Oh. fuck.

435
00:28:25.247 --> 00:28:26.707
- You've probably built a tolerance...
- [Anna] Max!

436
00:28:26.790 --> 00:28:28.959
- [Tom] No! Don't do that. Max! No!
- ...but don't worry because this.

437
00:28:29.042 --> 00:28:30.919
- this is a big one.
- No. no!

438
00:28:31.003 --> 00:28:32.296
[Max] Just a little pinch.

439
00:28:32.379 --> 00:28:33.505
[Tom] No!

440
00:28:33.589 --> 00:28:35.299
- [Max] Wow. he goes fast.
- [Anna] Just look at me.

441
00:28:35.382 --> 00:28:37.342
I'm right here. Okay? I'm right here.

442
00:28:37.426 --> 00:28:39.094
- [Max] Look at that.
- [Anna] I'm right here.

443
00:28:39.178 --> 00:28:40.470
[Max] Come here.

444
00:28:45.184 --> 00:28:46.476
[Max. muffled] Okay. like that.

445
00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:52.733
[normal] All right. now we have
the whole family together. Finally.

446
00:28:53.400 --> 00:28:54.818
But. before we get started.

447
00:28:54.902 --> 00:28:59.656
Tom. thank you so very much
for raising my kids. [laughing]

448
00:29:00.240 --> 00:29:01.658
[Anna] Is that what you want to hear?

449
00:29:01.742 --> 00:29:03.827
Y-You want me to say
that she's your daughter.

450
00:29:03.911 --> 00:29:05.370
she's your daughter. She...

451
00:29:05.454 --> 00:29:07.289
He-He's your son. You made him your son.

452
00:29:07.915 --> 00:29:10.501
Okay? Okay. you win. Just let them leave.

453
00:29:10.584 --> 00:29:12.503
- I can't let them leave.
- [Anna] No. you should let them leave.

454
00:29:12.586 --> 00:29:14.171
I can't let them leave because...

455
00:29:14.254 --> 00:29:15.464
Hey. stop it.

456
00:29:15.547 --> 00:29:18.050
If I let them leave. I don't have my jury.

457
00:29:18.133 --> 00:29:20.511
- All rise.
- [whimpers]

458
00:29:21.386 --> 00:29:25.474
The People
versus Anna Deveraux and Tom Bowden

459
00:29:26.099 --> 00:29:27.434
is now in session.

460
00:29:27.935 --> 00:29:31.688
So. lady and little gentleman of the jury.

461
00:29:32.189 --> 00:29:38.612
the evidence will show
that Ms. Deveraux and Mr. Bowden conspired

462
00:29:38.695 --> 00:29:41.406
to send Max Cady to prison
for their own personal reasons.

463
00:29:41.490 --> 00:29:43.492
Sit down. Hey. you got a Bible?

464
00:29:44.201 --> 00:29:45.494
What?

465
00:29:45.577 --> 00:29:47.871
Move to strike. Your Honor.

466
00:29:47.955 --> 00:29:50.123
- [grunts. groans]
- Bible.

467
00:29:50.207 --> 00:29:53.293
[stammers] They're usually black
with a cross on it.

468
00:29:53.377 --> 00:29:54.586
What the fuck are you doing?

469
00:29:54.670 --> 00:29:56.922
[Max] What the fuck am I doing?
Take a look at this.

470
00:29:57.589 --> 00:29:58.590
Hey.

471
00:29:59.758 --> 00:30:02.052
I want you to bite off your tongue for me.

472
00:30:02.135 --> 00:30:03.720
Zack. don't listen!

473
00:30:03.804 --> 00:30:04.847
Ah.

474
00:30:04.930 --> 00:30:07.432
- No. no. no. Zack. Zack. Zack.
- Zack. don't do it. No!

475
00:30:07.516 --> 00:30:09.518
- Bite down really slow. [hums]
- [Tom] Zack! Zack!

476
00:30:09.601 --> 00:30:10.769
- [Anna] Zack! [gasps]
- [Tom] No.

477
00:30:11.353 --> 00:30:14.273
- [Max] A little bit stronger. Keep going.
- [Anna] Okay. okay. okay. I swear.

478
00:30:14.356 --> 00:30:15.482
I-I-I swear to tell the truth.

479
00:30:15.566 --> 00:30:16.859
We swear to tell the whole truth. Max.

480
00:30:16.942 --> 00:30:18.318
[Anna] I swear to tell the whole truth.

481
00:30:18.402 --> 00:30:22.072
Okay. okay. okay. Boy. boy. boy.
Okay. wait for a second. Good job.

482
00:30:23.031 --> 00:30:24.241
Ms. Deveraux.

483
00:30:26.118 --> 00:30:31.623
Tell the jury the truth about
the deal you told Maximiliano Cady

484
00:30:32.332 --> 00:30:33.375
that he should take.

485
00:30:33.876 --> 00:30:36.753
- I... I got you a deal...
- [Max] Mm-hmm.

486
00:30:36.837 --> 00:30:38.714
...to take the death penalty off the table.

487
00:30:38.797 --> 00:30:41.049
Let me remind the witness
she's under oath.

488
00:30:41.133 --> 00:30:42.718
That is exactly what happened. Max.

489
00:30:42.801 --> 00:30:45.929
Permission to treat the other witness
as hostile. Your Honor.

490
00:30:46.013 --> 00:30:47.681
- [groans]
- [Anna] Tom.

491
00:30:47.764 --> 00:30:49.266
Okay. okay. okay. we conspired.

492
00:30:49.349 --> 00:30:50.934
Is that what you want to hear?
We made it up.

493
00:30:51.018 --> 00:30:55.314
What I want to hear is the truth. Anna.
For once in your fucking life. one truth.

494
00:30:57.733 --> 00:30:58.734
Okay.

495
00:30:58.817 --> 00:31:00.819
[suspenseful music playing]

496
00:31:06.325 --> 00:31:09.077
